# Alterra — GUI/Model Merge: Current State & Rewrite Plan

Single reference document for the in-progress branch merge. Written from a
file-by-file audit across multiple dev branches (batches sent and reviewed
in chat, not yet all applied to disk). Supersedes nothing else in `docs/`
— this covers only the merge/rewrite itself.

**Goal restated precisely**: one GUI entry point that exposes every
capability built so far — live single-episode playback, scenario
selection (preset + custom-mix), model import/registry, and the
multi-scheduler comparison — as tabs/pages of one running app, not
separate ad-hoc builds.

---

## 1. Confirmed bugs (fix regardless of anything else)

### 1.1 `simulation/environment/__init__.py` missing exports
Current content only exports `BandOccupancy, SpectrumWorld, Detection,
SensorModel, DwellResult, Receiver, AlterraEnv, PulseDescriptorWord,
generate_episode_pdws, band_center_hz`.

A separate, unused file `environment_init.py` has the same content **plus**:
```python
from .traditional_scanner import (
    BALANCED_RANDOM, SEQUENTIAL, TraditionalScanDriver,
    TraditionalScanner, run_traditional_scan,
)
```
`interfaces/cli/cli_main.py` does `from simulation.environment import
AlterraEnv, run_traditional_scan` — this **will raise `ImportError` as the
tree currently stands**. `comparison.py`'s traditional job path and any
GUI code driving `TraditionalScanDriver` directly need the same exports.

**Fix**: replace `__init__.py`'s content with `environment_init.py`'s
(shown above, merged), then delete `environment_init.py` so there's one
file, not two.

### 1.2 `pyproject.toml` entry point points at the stale CLI file
```toml
[project.scripts]
alterra = "interfaces.cli.main:cli"
```
`interfaces/cli/main.py` is the **old** file — no `env compare` command,
no `apply_overrides`/`run_traditional_scan` imports.
`interfaces/cli/cli_main.py` is current (superset of `main.py` plus
`compare`). The installed `alterra` command currently runs the stale one.

**Fix**: pick one filename and make it so on disk + in `pyproject.toml`.
Two options, functionally identical either way:
- (a) Delete `main.py`, rename `cli_main.py` → `main.py`, keep
  `pyproject.toml` as-is.
- (b) Delete `main.py`, keep `cli_main.py`'s name, change
  `pyproject.toml` to `interfaces.cli.cli_main:cli`.

Not resolved in this doc — see open questions §6.

