## 2. Python side: confirmed current, no action needed

Every file below was checked line-for-line against what's on disk in the
`hybrid-scheduler` branch and matches exactly — not stale, not
superseded, nothing to reconcile:

`simulation/emitters/{agile,base,fixed,periodic_scan}_emitter.py`,
`emitter_factory.py`, `scenario_builder.py`, `schedule_utils.py`,
`simulation/environment/{doctrine,comparison,scheduler_insight,
sensor_model,spectrum_world,receiver,traditional_scanner,
pdw_export,gym_env}.py`, `simulation/metrics/rollout_metrics.py`,
`simulation/utils/{config_loader,rng}.py`, `simulation/viz/spectrogram_plot.py`,
`model/agents/{heuristic_scheduler,evaluate,evaluate_hybrid,gui_comparison,
inspect_policy,model_registry,policy_runner,train_hybrid,train_ppo}.py`,
`model/deinterleaving/{dataset,losses,model,train}.py`,
`pyproject.toml` (content correct, just the one entry-point line wrong —
§1.2), `requirements.txt`.

### 2.1 Notable capabilities already built but not yet GUI-wired
These exist and work (used by CLI/eval scripts) but nothing in either
GUI iteration calls them yet:
- `AlterraEnv.band_priorities()` → `scheduler_insight.compute_band_priorities()`
  — per-band priority score, visit/hit counts, confidence, threat level,
  staleness. This is exactly what `MainWindow.ui`'s **Priority Map** tab
  (`priorityTable`, 7 columns: Band/Freq/Priority/Visits/Hits/
  Confidence/Threat) needs.
- `AlterraEnv.recent_events(n)` / `recent_hits(n)` →
  `SchedulerHistory` — per-decision history with `DecisionExplanation`
  (explore/exploit label, reason, priority score), classification counts,
  mean power. This is what the **events table** and **Recent Detections**
  tab need.
- `scheduler_insight.explain_decision()` → `DecisionExplanation` — this is
  what `MainWindow.ui`'s decision strip (`currentBandLabel`,
  `priorityScoreLabel`, `decisionValueLabel`, `reasonValueLabel`) needs.
  `AlterraEnv.step()`'s `info` dict already carries `decision`,
  `decision_reason`, `priority_score` — just needs to reach the GUI.
- `apply_overrides()` (`config_loader.py`) — episode-length override,
  fixed emitter count, traditional-scan mode/dwell overrides. This is
  what `episodeLengthSpin`/`applyConfigButton` and
  `traditionalDwellSpin` need.
- `scenario_builder.build_custom_population()` + archetype catalog
  (`fixed_low/medium/high`, `mid_episode_burst`, `silent_gap_revisit`,
  `fast_hopper`, `periodic_scanner`, `"random"`) + `config_overrides`
  support (`apply_scenario_overrides`, e.g. boosted `pfa_rate`) — no
  confirmed GUI surface found yet. See open question §6.3.

